course: dictionary
lesson: 11775
title: Strong feeling words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words show how loudly or strongly someone is feeling. «Bawling» is one of them. When you meet it, picture the scene: the sound, the face, the noise. Then read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «The baby was bawling in the pram, so Mum rocked it gently.» A baby cannot hold back its feelings, and Mum is trying to calm it. So bawling means crying very loudly.
explain: «Dad was bawling at the boys for breaking the window.» There are no tears here. Dad is shouting roughly and angrily, so bawling can also mean shouting at someone. Always ask: who is making the noise, and why?
explain: Bawling is a strong, slightly informal word. Use it in stories to help the reader hear the noise. It is not a word for a quiet, gentle sort of crying.
fact: «Bawling» means crying very loudly, like a baby or an upset child.
fact: «Bawling» can also mean shouting loudly and roughly at someone.
fact: «Bawl someone out» means to tell them off angrily. This phrase is mainly used in the US.
fact: «Bawling your eyes out» means crying very hard and for a long time.
fact: «Bawling» is a little informal, so it suits stories and talk more than formal letters.
exercise: «The baby was bawling in the pram.» What does bawling mean here? | Laughing at the dog | Singing a soft song | *Crying very loudly | Sleeping peacefully
exercise: «Dad was bawling at the boys for breaking the window.» What is Dad doing? | *Shouting roughly and angrily at them | Whispering a secret | Reading a book quietly | Hugging them warmly
exercise: «She was bawling her eyes out after the film.» What does this mean? | She was sleeping in her seat | *She was crying very hard and for a long time | She was laughing at the film | She was singing along to the music
test: «The angry coach was bawling at the team after the match.» What does bawling suggest here? | Whispering kind words | *Shouting roughly and angrily | Crying softly with a smile | Cheering loudly for the team
test: What does «bawl someone out» mean? | *To tell them off angrily | To help them with their homework | To give them a present | To wave goodbye to them
exam: Which word could replace bawling in «The lost puppy was bawling for its mum» if you keep the same meaning? | Giggling | Sleeping | Whispering | *Wailing
